<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich Friedrich Karl vom Stein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1757">1757</a>–<a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Baron vom Stein, Karl vom Stein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich Friedrich Karl vom und zum Stein was a Prussian statesman who, as chief minister in 1807–08, began the reforms that rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> after its defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. His October Edict of 1807 abolished hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a>, and his municipal ordinance of 1808 introduced town self-government. Dismissed under French pressure, he later advised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> and helped organise the war of liberation against Napoleon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-friedrich-karl-vom-stein.jpg" alt="Heinrich Friedrich Karl vom Stein" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Christoph Rincklake · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portr%C3%A4t_des_Freiherrn_Karl_vom_und_zum_Stein_als_preu%C3%9Fischer_Minister.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After 1806 the reforms of <b>Karl vom Stein</b> and Karl August von Hardenberg created ministries, municipal self-government and a freer economy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
